        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1181">

                <pb facs="0866" n="790" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg790"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.113/4136</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Governor of California to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Executive Office</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Sacramento</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am just in receipt of your communication
                    of April 26, suggesting that the appropriate officials of this State be
                    instructed to cooperate with the agents of the Federal Government in the effort
                    to prevent the illegal carrying of arms and munitions of war into Mexico. Of
                    course, I shall cheerfully do everything possible in the premises, and will be
                    very glad to comply with any specific suggestions that you may make.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hiram W. Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
